{
  "ideas": [
    {
      "id": 15,
      "name": "Vine Swing",
      "approach": "handmade",
      "approachWhy": "Each rope chain has to be tuned by hand so the release always lands (rope length, swing speed and gap decide the throw); a random mix of those three would easily make throws that miss by a stud. 19 hand-made chains cover the three tiers with clear, different twists.",
      "engine": {
        "have": [
          "swing motion kind (pendulum on server time, amp + arm + period + phase), used by Blob Pendulums",
          "rope look (thin rod) and blob look (the grab knob at the rope end)",
          "slide motion (for anchors that move) and red see-through goo hazard look",
          "jelly connectors so each section starts and ends with a jump",
          "flip motion (for a rope that goes see-through for a while)",
          "melt trigger from Melting Floor (local player touches it, it cracks, darkens and drops after a hold time), reused for the Snapping Vine"
        ],
        "new": [
          {
            "what": "hazard touch = back to the start pad (the shared one from Crusher Alley); the goo pit under every chain uses it",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "swing axis option: today a swing only goes across the course (z); vines need it to swing along the course (x)",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "client grab controller: touching the rope's lower knob attaches you, you ride the rope end on server time, jump lets go with the rope end's speed plus a jump kick; a short no-grab time after letting go so you don't re-grab the same rope. Build it on the same 'held by a prop, jump lets go' base as Aim the Cannon's cannon seat controller, so both share one client piece",
            "size": "L"
          },
          {
            "what": "two motions on one part (anchor slides while the rope swings): the same system Merry-go-round plans as 'Wobble' (spin plus rock on one part), not a second one",
            "size": "M"
          },
          {
            "what": "course tests: a 'swing' step kind built on Climb's planned 'grab' step kind (reach from a ledge to a part over the void), adding a release check: rope-end speed at release plus jump kick must land on the next rope, pad or ladder with 20 % spare, so the gap test doesn't flag the 14 to 22 stud gaps",
            "size": "M"
          },
          {
            "what": "vine look: reuse Climb's goo ladder look (dripping green goo, handprints, squelch on grab) on the rope and knob; plus a 'sweet spot' flash where the knob glows green in the window where letting go lands (easy tier only) and a creak that ticks at the top of each swing",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "\"Jump to let go\" hint while hanging (phone-sized screen label, shown the first few times only)",
            "size": "S"
          }
        ]
      },
      "readability": "Every vine is a dripping green goo rope with a fat knob and handprints at the bottom (the same goo look as Climb's ladders, so 'green goo = grab it' reads across the course); touching it makes a squelch and you hang. While you hang a \"Jump to let go\" hint shows, the rope creaks at the top of each swing and a whoosh plays when you let go.",
